Python List Methods

This project is a simple Python exercise for learning how to work with Lists and use different list methods.

The program creates a list of team members and performs several operations, including removing an item, adding a new item, sorting the list, reversing its order, and counting the number of elements.

Topics Covered

- Creating a List in Python
- Using "remove()" to remove an element
- Using "append()" to add an element
- Using "sort()" to sort the list
- Using "reverse()" to reverse the list
- Using "len()" to count the number of elements
- Using "f-strings" to format output

Project Goal

The goal of this exercise is to understand how to modify, sort, reverse, and count elements in a Python list.

Language: Python 🐍
